{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Activation Handler CI/CD Pipeline",
  "description": "Automatically deploy activation handler when modified using Kiro agent hooks",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileSaved",
    "filePattern": "src/lambda/activation-handler/**"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "🚀 **Activation Handler CI/CD Pipeline Triggered**\n\nThe activation handler has been modified. Please execute this comprehensive CI/CD workflow using Kiro agent capabilities:\n\n**🔍 Step 1: Change Detection & Validation**\n1. Confirm that files in `src/lambda/activation-handler/` were modified\n2. Show me the specific files that changed\n3. Display a brief summary of the changes (git diff)\n4. Validate that the changes are related to activation handler logic\n\n**🧪 Step 2: Code Quality & Testing**\n5. Run TypeScript compilation: `npm run build`\n6. Run ESLint validation: `npm run lint`\n7. Execute test suite: `npm test`\n8. If any step fails, stop the pipeline and report the issues\n9. If all pass, confirm code quality is validated ✅\n\n**📝 Step 3: Git Operations**\n10. Check git status for uncommitted changes\n11. If uncommitted changes exist:\n    - Stage the activation handler files: `git add src/lambda/activation-handler/`\n    - Create a semantic commit: `git commit -m \"feat(activation-handler): [describe the change]\"`\n    - Ask for confirmation before pushing\n12. Push to GitHub: `git push origin recovered`\n13. Confirm the push was successful\n\n**🔧 Step 4: AWS Deployment via MCP**\n14. Use the AWS Operations MCP server to:\n    - Check current Lambda function status: `FOD-Compute-dev-ActivationHandler`\n    - Get the function's current configuration and last modified time\n    - Trigger the GitHub Actions workflow for activation handler deployment\n15. Monitor the deployment progress using AWS Operations MCP\n16. Wait for deployment completion (check every 30 seconds, max 5 minutes)\n\n**✅ Step 5: Deployment Verification**\n17. Use AWS Operations MCP server to:\n    - Verify the Lambda function was updated (check LastModified timestamp)\n    - Get the function's current state and configuration\n    - Check CloudWatch metrics for any immediate errors\n    - Confirm the function is in 'Active' state\n18. Use the Snapdragon Simulator MCP to:\n    - Test the activation flow if possible\n    - Verify the simulator can communicate with the updated function\n\n**📊 Step 6: Health Check & Monitoring**\n19. Run comprehensive health checks:\n    - Check Lambda function metrics (invocations, errors, duration)\n    - Verify API Gateway endpoints are responding\n    - Test the activation handler with a sample payload if safe\n20. Use AWS Operations MCP to get recent CloudWatch logs\n21. Look for any error patterns or warnings in the logs\n\n**📋 Step 7: Documentation & Reporting**\n22. Use GitHub MCP server to:\n    - Create a deployment record as a GitHub issue with:\n      - Title: \"Deployment: Activation Handler v[timestamp]\"\n      - Body: Include deployment details, function ARN, and verification results\n      - Labels: ['deployment', 'activation-handler', 'automated']\n23. Update any relevant documentation if the API changed\n24. Close any GitHub issues that were resolved by this deployment\n\n**🎉 Step 8: Completion Summary**\n25. Provide a comprehensive deployment summary:\n    - ✅ Code Quality: [PASSED/FAILED]\n    - ✅ Git Operations: [COMPLETED]\n    - ✅ AWS Deployment: [SUCCESS/FAILED]\n    - ✅ Function Status: [ACTIVE/ERROR]\n    - ✅ Health Checks: [PASSED/FAILED]\n    - 📊 Function ARN: `arn:aws:lambda:us-east-1:account:function:FOD-Compute-dev-ActivationHandler`\n    - 🕐 Deployment Time: [timestamp]\n    - 🔗 GitHub Actions URL: [workflow run URL]\n    - 📝 GitHub Issue: [deployment record issue URL]\n\n**🚨 Error Handling**\n- If any step fails, immediately stop the pipeline\n- Report the specific error and suggested remediation\n- Do not proceed to AWS deployment if code quality checks fail\n- If deployment fails, attempt rollback if possible\n- Always create a GitHub issue documenting any failures\n\n**🎯 Success Criteria**\n- All code quality checks pass\n- Git operations complete successfully\n- AWS Lambda function is updated and active\n- Health checks show no errors\n- Deployment is documented in GitHub\n\n**Important Notes:**\n- This hook uses Kiro's MCP servers (AWS Operations, GitHub, Snapdragon Simulator)\n- The deployment targets only the activation handler for faster deployment\n- All operations are logged and documented automatically\n- The pipeline follows AWS security best practices\n- Rollback procedures are available if deployment fails\n\nPlease execute this Kiro-powered CI/CD pipeline and keep me informed of each step's progress. Use the MCP servers to perform the actual operations rather than traditional scripts."
  },
  "workspaceFolderName": "snapdragon-fod-aws",
  "shortName": "activation-handler-cicd"
}